      "text": "The height of the prism is 16, which means that points $A$ and $S$, the topmost vertex of the prism, are separated by the length of 16 units. To determine the length of $X$ in the triangle $ABC$, starting with point $A$ and drawing a straight line of $16$ between the top $S$ and bottom vertex $A$, a perpendicular line of $8$ from the top to $X$ is required. As $X$ and $Y$ are the midpoints of $AC$ and $BC$ respectively, $X$ is located 6 units in from $A$ and 6 units in from $B$. Using the proximity of $A$ and the calculated value for $X$, the vector $\\overrightarrow{BX}$ is $(6-6, 0-8) = (0,-8)$. The distance of this particular line from the $X$ vector can be found using the Pythagorean Theorem with the hypotenuse $=\\sqrt{16^2+8^2}=\\sqrt{400}=20$. The perimeter of $XYZ$ is then calculated by adding the length of $XY$, which is $\\sqrt{(8^2+6^2)}=\\sqrt{100}=10$, then $X$ and $Y$ made up at $20$ units. The perimeter is $10+20=30$ units [asy]\ndraw((0,-20)--(6,-6)--(12,-6));\ndraw((0,-6)--(0,-20)--(12,-6));\n//\ndraw((0,-20)--(0,0));\ndraw((0,0)--(6,-6));\ndraw((12,-6)--(6,-6));\n//\ndraw((6,-6)--(6,0));\n//\ndraw((0,-5.5)--(6,-6.5));\ndraw((0, 3)--(6, -2.5));\ndraw((3.5,0)--(3.5,-5.5));\ndraw((3,-6)--(3,-2));\n//\nlabel(\" $A$ \",(0,-20),SW);\nlabel(\" $S$ \",(6,-6),NW);\nlabel(\" $X$ \",(3,-6),SW);\nlabel(\" $Y$ \",(6,-6),NE);\nlabel(\" $Z$ \",(12,-6),SE);\nlabel(\" $C$ \",(6,-6),S);\nlabel(\" $D$ \",(12,-6),S);\nlabel(\" $B$ \",(6,0),E);\n[/asy] The answer is 30",
