      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To find the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) in the given right prism, we need to determine the lengths of the sides \\(XY\\), \\(YZ\\), and \\(ZX\\).\n\n1. **Calculate the coordinates of points \\(A\\), \\(B\\), and \\(C\\):**\n   - Point \\(A\\) is at \\((0,0)\\).\n   - Point \\(B\\) is at \\((12,0)\\).\n   - Point \\(C\\) is at \\((6,-6)\\).\n\n2. **Determine the midpoints \\(X\\), \\(Y\\), and \\(Z\\):**\n   - Point \\(X\\) is the midpoint of \\(AC\\):\n     \\[\n     X = \\left( \\frac{0+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2} \\right) = (3, -3)\n     \\]\n   - Point \\(Y\\) is the midpoint of \\(BC\\):\n     \\[\n     Y = \\left( \\frac{12+6}{2}, \\frac{0-6}{2} \\right) = (9, -3)\n     \\]\n   - Point \\(Z\\) is the midpoint of \\(CD\\):\n     \\[\n     Z = \\left( \\frac{6+0}{2}, \\frac{-6-22}{2} \\right) = (3, -14)\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the distances \\(XY\\), \\(YZ\\), and \\(ZX\\):**\n   - For \\(XY\\):\n     \\[\n     XY = \\sqrt{(9-3)^2 + (-3+3)^2} = \\sqrt{6^2} = 6\n     \\]\n   - For \\(YZ\\):\n     \\[\n     YZ = \\sqrt{(6-3)^2 + (-14+3)^2} = \\sqrt{3^2 + (-11)^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 121} = \\sqrt{130}\n     \\]\n   - For \\(ZX\\):\n     \\[\n     ZX = \\sqrt{(3-3)^2 + (-14+3)^2} = \\sqrt{0^2 + (-11)^2} = 11\n     \\]\n\n4. **Sum the lengths \\(XY\\), \\(YZ\\), and \\(ZX\\) to find the perimeter:**\n   \\[\n   XY + YZ + ZX = 6 + \\sqrt{130} + 11 = 17 + \\sqrt{130}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the perimeter of triangle \\(XYZ\\) is \\(\\boxed{17 + \\sqrt{130}}\\).",
